The plutonium-239 half-life exercise mixes unit typesetting mid-sentence:
the barrel's mass uses the correct `\text{kg}` unit macro ($10\,\text{kg}$)
but the remaining-mass quantity a few words later was left as bare `$10g$`,
which typesets "g" as an italic math variable multiplying 10 rather than as
the unit "grams". Fixed to `$10\,\text{g}$` to match the sibling quantity's
convention in the same sentence.

